# Project context
This is a Next.js 14 (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS website for a dental clinic
and its in-house dental laboratory, built by an agency/freelancer to be resold as a
reusable template across multiple clinic clients.

# Tone & content
- This is a medical/dental website. Tone must be professional, clean, calm, and
  trustworthy — never salesy, gimmicky, or overly casual.
- Never invent clinic details, doctor names, statistics, testimonials, or reviews that
  aren't present in `/content/site-data.json`. If an array in site-data.json is empty,
  render a graceful empty/hidden state — do not fabricate entries to "fill space."
- Never claim medical outcomes, guarantees, or make health claims not explicitly
  provided in the source content (e.g. don't write "guaranteed pain-free" unless that
  exact claim exists in site-data.json).

# Stack rules
- Always use TypeScript, never plain JS. No `any` types unless absolutely unavoidable
  (and then with a comment explaining why).
- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes for styling; do not write standalone CSS files
  unless Tailwind genuinely cannot achieve the effect (e.g. complex keyframe animation).
- Use shadcn/ui components as the base for buttons, cards, accordions, dialogs, toasts,
  and forms — do not hand-roll these primitives from scratch.
- Use `next/image` for all images and `next/font` for all fonts — never raw `<img>` tags
  or external font `<link>` tags.

# Single source of truth (critical)
- ALL content — names, phone numbers, addresses, hours, services, doctor bios, FAQs,
  testimonials, theme colors, image paths — must be imported from the typed `siteData`
  object exported by `/lib/get-site-data.ts`, which reads `/content/site-data.json`.
- Never hardcode a phone number, name, address, color hex value, or any client-specific
  string directly inside a component file.
- If a component needs a field that doesn't exist in site-data.json yet, add the field
  to the JSON and to `/lib/site-data-types.ts` first, then consume it through `siteData`.
  Do not inline it as a one-off "just this once."
- This rule exists so the entire site can be reused for a new client by editing one file
  and swapping images — never break that by scattering content into JSX.

# General code quality
- Prefer server components by default; only add `"use client"` when a component needs
  interactivity, state, or browser APIs (animations, forms, carousels, accordions).
- Keep components focused — one section per file inside `/components/sections`, shared
  UI (Navbar, Footer, WhatsApp button) inside `/components/shared`.
- Never commit real patient data, PII, or API keys into the repo. Secrets go in
  `.env.local` (gitignored) with a matching `.env.example` documenting the required keys.
